{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/484345-play-aides-gm-screen-condition-cards","id":484345,"title":"Play Aides (GM Screen & Condition Cards)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-18T00:44:15-07:00","id":484345,"title":"Play Aides (GM Screen & Condition Cards)","content":"I'm putting together a deck of condition/tilt cards (like <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/snzkT1u.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>) &amp; a GM screen for personal use. I was just wondering which ones would be alright to post for others to use without stepping on legal toes, 'cause I'm using a lot of the things from the book (all the tables, for the GM screen, for one). I'm already considering the GM screen vetoed, 'cause it's approximately 15 pages of the book condensed into three, but would the Condition/Tilt cards from W:tF be alright?<br /> <br /> When I'm finished with the W:tF ones, I'll be doing the WoD:GM ones, so I don't really have a problem with posting those, since the text is from a free pdf.... Maybe I should be doing those first.<br /> <br /> Also, if this gets vetoed in its' entirety, so that this topic isn't a total bust, check out <a href=\"http://cgjennings.ca/eons/\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Eons</a>. It's got a (relatively) good UI for making table top stuff like cards. It defaults it Arkham Horror, which I'm using for my condition cards, but has support for plugins so you can make other things, if you know java. Bit clunky, though.<br /> <br /> Also, input into Condition cards would be cool too. How would you make 'em? I want ideas to stop them from just being walls of text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe